# Keep Bazel out of Cargo output dirs and the detached Cargo workspaces under
# `tools/` (nip29-consumer, fjall probes). Same bug class as the .gitignore
# `target*` rule: a nested `target/` must never become a Bazel package.
target
**/target
crates/nmp-ui

# Agent worktrees live under `.claude/worktrees/<name>/`, INSIDE the primary
# checkout. Each is a full checkout carrying its own `bazel-*` convenience
# symlinks, and those point into that worktree's execroot -- which contains
# every external repo it fetched. Without this, `bazel test //...` run from
# the primary checkout walks into a sibling worktree's execroot and fails
# loading a package out of someone else's `@rules_shell`. Same bug class as
# `target` above: a nested build output must never become a Bazel package.
.claude